---
title: Lentil and Sausage Soup
course: main
cuisine: italian
servings: 4
time_active: 25
time_total: 65
leftovers: great
tags: [weeknight, one-pot, freezer-friendly]
pairs: [balsamic-brussels-sprouts]
description: Brown lentils simmered with Italian sausage, vegetables, and kale, finished with lemon and parmesan.
---

Heat @olive oil{1%tbsp} in a #dutch oven{} over medium-high. Add @Italian sausage{2/3%lb}(casings removed; chicken or turkey to keep it lighter) and cook, breaking it up, until browned, ~{6-8%minutes}. Move it to a plate with a slotted spoon, leaving the fat behind.

Lower the heat to medium. Add a diced @yellow onion{1}, @carrots{2}(diced), and @celery{2%stalk}(diced) with a pinch of @salt. Cook until soft, ~{8%minutes}.

Stir in @garlic{3%clove}(minced), @tomato paste{2%tbsp}, @dried thyme{1%tsp}, and @?red pepper flakes{1/2%tsp}. Cook until the paste darkens, ~{2%minutes}.

Add @brown lentils{1%cup}(rinsed), @diced tomatoes{1%can}(14.5 oz), @chicken broth{4%cups}, @bay leaves{2}, and the sausage. Bring to a boil, then simmer partly covered until the lentils are tender, ~{25-30%minutes}.

Remove the bay leaves. Stir in @lacinato kale{1%bunch}(stems removed, chopped) and simmer until wilted, ~{5%minutes}.

Stir in the juice of half a @lemon{1/2} and season with salt and @black pepper{}. Serve topped with chopped @?parsley{1/4%cup}(flat-leaf), grated @?parmesan{}, and a drizzle of olive oil.

> The soup thickens as it sits; thin leftovers with broth or water. Freezes well for up to 3 months, best frozen before adding the kale.
